---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — Streich Force Enterprises"
  description="Streich Force Enterprises privacy policy — how we collect, use, and protect your personal information.">
  <Nav />
  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="legal-inner">
      <p class="sf-eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Effective: June 6, 2023 &mdash; Last updated: September 10, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="legal-body">
    <div class="legal-inner">

      <p>Your privacy is important to us. It is Streich Force Enterprises' policy to respect your privacy and comply with any applicable law and regulation regarding any personal information we may collect about you, including across our website, https://streichforce.com/, and other sites we own and operate.</p>

      <p>Personal information is any information about you which can be used to identify you. This includes information about you as a person (such as name, address, and date of birth), your devices, payment details, and even information about how you use a website or online service.</p>

      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
      <p>Information we collect falls into one of two categories: "voluntarily provided" information and "automatically collected" information.</p>
      <p>"Voluntarily provided" information refers to any information you knowingly and actively provide us when using or participating in any of our services and promotions.</p>
      <p>"Automatically collected" information refers to any information automatically sent by your devices in the course of accessing our products and services.</p>

      <h2>Log Data</h2>
      <p>When you visit our website, our servers may automatically log the standard data provided by your web browser. It may include your device's Internet Protocol (IP) address, your browser type and version, the pages you visit, the time and date of your visit, the time spent on each page, and other details about your visit.</p>

      <h2>Personal Information</h2>
      <p>We may ask for personal information — for example, when you contact us through our forms — which may include one or more of the following:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Name</li>
        <li>Email address</li>
        <li>Phone number</li>
        <li>Company name and location</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Collection and Use of Information</h2>
      <p>We may collect personal information from you when you do any of the following on our website:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Submit a contact or quote request form</li>
        <li>Contact us via email or phone</li>
        <li>Use a mobile device or web browser to access our content</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may collect, hold, use, and disclose information for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your inquiry or service request</li>
        <li>To contact and communicate with you</li>
        <li>To provide you with information about our services</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Security of Your Personal Information</h2>
      <p>When we collect and process personal information, we will protect it within commercially acceptable means to prevent loss and theft, as well as unauthorized access, disclosure, copying, use, or modification. No method of electronic transmission or storage is 100% secure, and no one can guarantee absolute data security.</p>

      <h2>How Long We Keep Your Personal Information</h2>
      <p>We keep your personal information only for as long as we need to. If your personal information is no longer required, we will delete it or make it anonymous by removing all details that identify you.</p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>We do not aim any of our products or services directly at children under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information about children under 13.</p>

      <h2>Disclosure of Personal Information to Third Parties</h2>
      <p>We may disclose personal information to third-party service providers for the purpose of enabling them to provide their services, including IT service providers, data storage, hosting and server providers, and professional advisors. We do not sell your personal information to third parties.</p>

      <h2>Text Messages (SMS)</h2>
      <p>Streich Force Enterprises sends text messages to technicians, subcontractors and staff who have expressly opted in to receive them. These are operational messages about work assigned to you through SF Ops &mdash; a new job assignment, a schedule or deadline change, and occasional related account notices. They are not marketing messages.</p>
      <p>You opt in either by submitting our consent form at <a href="https://ops.streichforce.com/sms-opt-in">ops.streichforce.com/sms-opt-in</a> or by giving consent directly to an administrator. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to any message to stop receiving texts, or HELP for help. Consent is not a condition of employment or of any purchase, and you may withdraw it at any time.</p>
      <p><strong>No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.</strong> Mobile opt-in data and consent records are not sold, rented or shared with anyone, and are excluded from the third-party disclosures described above. The only exception is the messaging providers who deliver the messages on our behalf, who may not use the information for any other purpose.</p>
      <p>We keep a record of your consent &mdash; your name, mobile number, the date and the wording you agreed to &mdash; for as long as you are enrolled, and afterwards only as long as needed to show that consent was given.</p>

      <h2>Your Rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to access, correct, or request deletion of personal information we hold about you. To make such a request, contact us at <a href="mailto:info&#x40;streichforce.com">info&#x40;streichforce.com</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>At our discretion, we may change our privacy policy to reflect updates to our business processes or legislative changes. If we decide to change this privacy policy, we will post the changes here.</p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>For any questions or concerns regarding your privacy, contact us at:</p>
      <p>
        Streich Force Enterprises<br />
        <a href="mailto:info&#x40;streichforce.com">info&#x40;streichforce.com</a><br />
        <a href="tel:6024050031">602-405-0031</a>
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.legal-hero { padding: 8rem var(--sf-pad) 3rem; background: var(--sf-black); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sf-border); }
.legal-inner { max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; }
.legal-title { font-family: var(--sf-font-display); font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4rem); text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sf-text-primary); line-height: 1; margin: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem; }
.legal-meta { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--sf-text-muted); }
.legal-body { padding: 4rem var(--sf-pad) 7rem; background: var(--sf-surface); }
.legal-body p { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--sf-text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
.legal-body h2 { font-family: var(--sf-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.2rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sf-text-primary); margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
.legal-body ul { padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
.legal-body ul li { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--sf-text-secondary); line-height: 1.7; }
.legal-body a { color: var(--sf-rust); text-decoration: none; }
.legal-body a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
